  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 39. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 現状 — 今の状態や様子。\n2. 元素 — 物質を作る原子の種類。\n3. 幻想 — 実際にはないのに心の中に思い描く姿や世界。\n4. 現代 — 自分たちが生きている今の時代。\n5. 現地 — ある出来事などが起きているその場所。\n6. 限度 — それ以上は進めないとする範囲や境目。\n7. 言動 — 言ったことと行ったこと。\n8. 現場 — 実際に作業や出来事がある場所。\n9. 原理 — 物事が成り立つもとになる仕組みや決まり。\n10. ゲート — 出入りするための門や入口。\n11. ゲームセンター — いろいろな遊びの機械が置いてある店。\n12. コインロッカー — お金を払って荷物を預ける鍵付きの箱。\n13. 降雨 — 雨が降ること。\n14. 講演会 — 集まった人があるテーマについての話を聞く会。\n15. 公会堂 — 地域の人などが集会や催しに使う建物。\n16. 高気圧 — 周りより気圧が高いところ。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
